01:34:55.706 --> 01:34:58.706
I want my life to still be an offering to God.

741
01:34:58.706 --> 01:35:03.706
What is, for example, a sacrifice to God that we talked about last month?

742
01:35:03.706 --> 01:35:09.706
That you say to yourself, I am not going to do this thing that makes me briefly happy right now,

743
01:35:09.706 --> 01:35:14.706
of which I know that God says, do not do this. You know, instant gratification.

744
01:35:14.706 --> 01:35:17.706
But you say to yourself, you impose a sacrifice on yourself.

745
01:35:17.706 --> 01:35:21.706
You tell yourself no, I want to remain obedient to God,

746
01:35:21.706 --> 01:35:26.706
so that I can make God happy with my life, so that God can bless me.

747
01:35:26.706 --> 01:35:31.706
And so what I want to do in my life is, I want my life to be a sacrifice to the Lord.

748
01:35:31.706 --> 01:35:36.706
I just don't have to go to the Lord every time to give Him sorry sacrifices,

749
01:35:36.706 --> 01:35:38.706
because Jesus has done that for me.

750
01:35:42.706 --> 01:35:46.706
Hebrews chapter 10 verses 19 to 22 as a final point.

751
01:35:47.706 --> 01:35:55.706
Brothers and sisters, through the sacrificed blood of Jesus we can now enter the heavenly sanctuary without fear and full of faith

752
01:35:55.706 --> 01:35:57.706
and go into the presence of God. Jesus is the new and living way to God. Through that new way we can approach God.

753
01:35:57.706 --> 01:36:02.706
Behind the curtain that hangs before the heavenly Most Holy Place.

754
01:36:02.706 --> 01:36:06.706
Here are the bold words that I have underlined in my Bible.

755
01:36:06.706 --> 01:36:09.706
Jesus Himself, His body is that curtain.

756
01:36:09.706 --> 01:36:14.706
Only through Him can we enter. Can I get an amen on that?

757
01:36:14.706 --> 01:36:18.706
Shall we stand, for I will pray for us.

758
01:36:19.706 --> 01:36:21.706
Caroline, would you come up to the stage? We are going to sing a song.

759
01:36:28.706 --> 01:36:31.706
Verse 21, take a look with me, for we are going to conclude this sermon.

760
01:36:40.706 --> 01:36:44.706


761
01:36:46.706 --> 01:36:47.706
Verse 21.

762
01:36:47.706 --> 01:36:53.706
We have a mighty high priest over the house of God. Who is that?

763
01:36:53.706 --> 01:36:54.706
Jesus.

764
01:36:54.706 --> 01:37:00.706
Therefore, we can now approach God with a sincere heart and full confidence that He will receive us.

765
01:37:00.706 --> 01:37:06.706
For our heart has been cleansed by the blood of Jesus.

766
01:37:06.706 --> 01:37:08.706
Shall we close our eyes?

767
01:37:11.706 --> 01:37:15.706
Close your eyes for a moment and think about your own life.

768
01:37:17.706 --> 01:37:22.706
I always find it good during a prayer to come to self-reflection and be embedded.

769
01:37:22.706 --> 01:37:31.706
Self-reflection, that you think about yourself and with your eyes closed, because you can also talk to God now in connection with Him.

770
01:37:31.706 --> 01:37:35.706
Prayer is no different, it is as simple as having a conversation with God.

771
01:37:35.706 --> 01:37:37.706
Coming to God is a prayer.

772
01:37:38.706 --> 01:37:46.706
And when I ask in the church to close your eyes and come to self-reflection, the big question to everyone in this room at this moment is.

773
01:37:47.706 --> 01:37:51.706
Have you already accepted Jesus in your life?

774
01:37:52.706 --> 01:37:57.706
As Savior, who died on the cross for your sins.

775
01:37:59.706 --> 01:38:02.706
Or maybe even one step back, if you can't get there yet.

776
01:38:03.706 --> 01:38:09.706
If you think to yourself, this is intense information Tim, how do I accept Jesus and His blood in my life?

777
01:38:09.706 --> 01:38:11.706
I don't know.

778
01:38:11.706 --> 01:38:13.706
Here is step one.

779
01:38:14.706 --> 01:38:17.706
Do you know that you are a sinner?

780
01:38:17.706 --> 01:38:19.706
I know this about myself.

781
01:38:19.706 --> 01:38:21.706
I know that I have made mistakes.

782
01:38:21.706 --> 01:38:23.706
I know that I have caused pain to others.

783
01:38:23.706 --> 01:38:26.706
I know that I have been dishonest in my life.

784
01:38:26.706 --> 01:38:28.706
I know that I have been disobedient to God.

785
01:38:28.706 --> 01:38:31.706
I know for myself that I am a sinner.

786
01:38:32.706 --> 01:38:36.706
But I also know for myself that I have accepted Jesus into my life.

787
01:38:36.706 --> 01:38:39.706
And that I have put an end to my sinful life.

788
01:38:39.706 --> 01:38:44.706
So that I can be cleansed by the blood of Jesus from all the sins I have committed.

789
01:38:44.706 --> 01:38:47.706
And even the mistakes that I still make.

790
01:38:48.706 --> 01:38:52.706
Everyone keep your eyes closed, for this is a prayer for all of us.

791
01:38:52.706 --> 01:38:55.706
Even the mistakes that you still make.

792
01:38:55.706 --> 01:39:00.706
This is not a free pass for our church to live hypocritically together.

793
01:39:00.706 --> 01:39:03.706
And that we can just continue with our sin in our lives.

794
01:39:03.706 --> 01:39:08.706
And that we can say, well if it's that easy, then I will just ask for forgiveness from Jesus every time.

795
01:39:08.706 --> 01:39:10.706
Because He has done it, then I can continue living.

796
01:39:10.706 --> 01:39:13.706
This is not being cleansed by the blood of Jesus.

797
01:39:14.706 --> 01:39:18.706
Jesus wants to cleanse you with His blood, so that you can live for God.

798
01:39:18.706 --> 01:39:20.706
And that you can have a blessed life.

799
01:39:20.706 --> 01:39:22.706
And that you can have a hopeful future.

800
01:39:22.706 --> 01:39:26.706
And that you can live with God in glory and worship to Him.

801
01:39:27.706 --> 01:39:30.706
But my question at the end of this service is.

802
01:39:30.706 --> 01:39:34.706
Do you know that you can be forgiven by the blood of Jesus?

803
01:39:34.706 --> 01:39:38.706
That all the mistakes, the relative mistakes that have happened.

804
01:39:38.706 --> 01:39:40.706
The mistakes that have happened in your family.

805
01:39:40.706 --> 01:39:42.706
The mistakes that have happened in your marriage.

806
01:39:42.706 --> 01:39:45.706
The mistakes that have been done to you in your family.

807
01:39:45.706 --> 01:39:48.706
The mistakes you have made out of selfishness, the lies.

808
01:39:48.706 --> 01:39:51.706
All things, the gossip, everything, everything, everything.

809
01:39:51.706 --> 01:39:56.706
All your sins can be forgiven by the blood of King Jesus.

810
01:39:57.706 --> 01:40:02.706
And I ask everyone to close their eyes, because I just want to pray for people.

811
01:40:02.706 --> 01:40:06.706
I just want to pray for you, that you accept Jesus in your life.

812
01:40:06.706 --> 01:40:09.706
Simply put, accept Jesus in your life.

813
01:40:09.706 --> 01:40:11.706
Continue with God.

814
01:40:13.706 --> 01:40:19.706
Have you accepted God as your personal Redeemer?

815
01:40:19.706 --> 01:40:22.706
Lord, I want to pray for everyone in this room.

816
01:40:22.706 --> 01:40:26.706
Lord, that as we go on with our week, as we go through life,

817
01:40:26.706 --> 01:40:28.706
that we know that Jesus is for us.

818
01:40:28.706 --> 01:40:30.706
That He is not against us.

819
01:40:30.706 --> 01:40:34.706
But that He has washed us clean, so that we can be children of God.

820
01:40:35.706 --> 01:40:38.706
Lord, I want to pray over this church, for all of us.

821
01:40:38.706 --> 01:40:42.706
Lord, that our lives will be for Him.

822
01:40:42.706 --> 01:40:46.706
That we can make God happy, through the blood of Jesus.

823
01:40:48.706 --> 01:40:51.706
And lastly, I want to say, church, accept Jesus.

824
01:40:51.706 --> 01:40:53.706
Accept Him today.

825
01:40:53.706 --> 01:40:56.706
Do not wait until tomorrow. Do not clean up your life first.

826
01:40:56.706 --> 01:40:58.706
But accept Him today.

827
01:40:58.706 --> 01:41:00.706
Today is the day of salvation.

828
01:41:01.706 --> 01:41:03.706
Today is the day of salvation, in Jesus' name.

829
